 - Adobe red (#EB1000), black and white, Source Sans 3 like the video page, the Adobe logo in the masthead. The SOW document itself carries the partner's name and no Adobe logo: it's the partner's paper to its customer.
 - Nothing about Adobe Consulting Services.
 
+## Figma connects to AEM Assets, GenStudio for Performance Marketing, Adobe Express and Firefly Custom Models (November 17, 2026)
+
+Figma, the outside system added for Brand Intelligence on November 16, connects to four more products, each through a plugin or add-on Adobe documents, drawn as native lines like Figma + Brand Intelligence and Adobe Asset Link: **AEM Assets** (Adobe's AEM Assets Connector places AEM Assets files on the Figma canvas and saves designs back), **GenStudio for Performance Marketing** (Adobe's GenStudio plugin, which opens in Figma as the Firefly Enterprise and GenStudio plugin, generates on-brand ad variations in Figma templates and exports them to GenStudio; the card is for clients whose designers already work in Figma), **Adobe Express** (the Figma add-on in Express imports Figma pages, frames or layers) and **Firefly Custom Models** (custom models are picked in Text to image in the Firefly Enterprise and GenStudio plugin). Every quote behind the cards was checked word for word on Experience League and Adobe Help on November 17, and the cards show those pages as links only. Following the owner's November 12 rule (step 86), nothing on them asks the partner to confirm anything with Adobe. No Adobe page read names who publishes the Figma add-on in Express.
+
+Six optional services start off, like XK16, so a canvas saved before them reopens with the same services and totals: XF01 AEM Assets Connector rollout for Figma designers and XF02 Save-back folders and export settings for Figma designs (8 / 16 / 32 hours each), XF03 Figma ad templates prepared for the GenStudio plugin (16 / 32 / 56), XF04 Figma frames converted for GenStudio Photoshop (8 / 16 / 32; it also needs GenStudio Photoshop in Photoshop 25.6.0 or later), XF05 Figma designs turned into Express templates (16 / 24 / 48) and XF06 Custom models for Figma designers (8 / 16 / 24). Each keeps its own deliverable beside the services it touches (AS01, AS02, XJ03, GS03, XJ10, EP03, FM03 to FM05, XK09, XK10); `canvas/research/wave6_figma.json` says how, with the quotes. The rest of the data is in `canvas/research/connection_types.json`, `product_copy_rules.json` (the client's version and the supporting pages) and the RFI write-ups in `rfp_prototype/kb_method` (batch 14). The statement of work keeps Figma on Create your own play (`OUTSIDE_MORE` in `index.html`), so a draft saved there and opened again brings Figma back with its chosen services (before, it came back without Figma, and the next save dropped XK16), and the RFI Builder names Figma when an RFI does (`NAMES` in `rfp_answers.js`). The catalog is 161 connections and 543 services; the counts move in `qa/check_product_copy.py`, `canvas/test_canvas.js` and `test_step61`, `62`, `64`, `66`, `71`, `85` and `91`. `canvas/test_canvas.js` checks the four connections and Figma on a canvas, and `test_step64.js` checks that a Figma service reaches the statement of work and comes back from a saved draft, and that the RFI Builder answers a question about Figma from the Figma services.
+
 ## Brand Intelligence connects to Creative Cloud and Coworker (November 17, 2026)
 
 Adam: "yes for both". The two connections that waited on November 16 are built as native connections with no services of their own. Both rest on Adobe's Brand validation page (https://business.adobe.com/products/brand-intelligence/validate.html), read from the owner's saved copy and screenshot because Adobe's business site blocks automated tools.
